ignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible in: 4.4.1.stable.fedora.49a5bc7b6, 4.5-beta7\n\n### System information\n\nFedora 42 - 4.4.1.stable.fedora.49a5bc7b6 - Forward+ and Compatibility - 16 × AMD Ryzen 7 PRO 7840U w/ Radeon 780M Graphics\n\n### Issue description\n\nTiles from one `TileMapLayer` are drawn on top of my character, but tiles from another `TileMapLayer` (with the exact same `y_sort` origin and `z_index`) are drawn below my character.\n\nI expect two tiles from two different `TileMapLayers` with the same `z_index` and `y_sort` origin to be drawn at the same time in relation to my character.\n\nI've double checked that everything has `y_sort` enabled and has the same `z_index`.\n\n<img width=\"1157\" height=\"652\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a3f679ea-b82a-4956-b2eb-05be248c5ac9\" />\n\n<img width=\"1152\" height=\"646\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c3c95dd9-9737-4414-9a6b-f3ee34b8b2a4\" />\n\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nCreated a minimal player node and two TileMapLayers.\n\nJust walk into the walls and you'll see -- some walls are drawn on top of the player's head, but the rubble (from the same TileMapLayer) seems to be working.\n\nI've included two tiles from a different TileMapLayer off to the side -- same y_sort origin and z_index, but these working as expected.\n\nI've added a picture to point to the exact tiles I'm talking about.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[test.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/22163663/test.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"engeljohnb","id":86657420,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2NjU3NDIw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/86657420?v=4","gravatar_id":"","u